THE WHOLE-HOUSE SHEET GUARD - RED-PROVED 24 Nov 2026 14:4x CT (art lane).

THE DEFECT (found by the team lead by LOOKING, while every number said GREEN):
  _hero_scale.png on main was 2280x10080 and became 2280x560 - ONE cell over a
  canvas two thirds empty - because the 14:03 `--only iceman` run passed its own
  single key into sheet() and overwrote the master. _contact_sheet.png and
  _silhouettes.png kept all 54 rows the same run because minibossgen.py writes
  them over all of ORDER; that asymmetry is the proof it was a bug.
  THE SAME ROOT CAUSE SHRANK THE CHECK: that run's blank_check opened 3 of 162
  view PNGs and reported 0 failures beside a verdict covering 56 rows.
  The 20 Nov ratcatcher note already knew the cause and the answer then was a
  second `--sheet` pass BY HAND. I forgot it. A fix that needs the operator to
  remember is not a fix.

THE FIX (tools/art/minibossfit.py, the sheet() call site):
  the master name `_hero_scale` now covers list(M.ORDER) whatever `--only` asked
  for; a sheet asked for under its own --name keeps the caller's keys.
  blank_check now reports cells/expected_files/scope, and RED ON EMPTY: a check
  that opened fewer files than the sheet has cells cannot report green.

AFTER: 2280x10080, 18 rows x 3 cols, 54 of 54 slots carry a body (lowest
  non-background count 66,612 px), 0 empty slots. blank_check 162 files /
  162 expected / 0 failures / scope whole_house. verdict GREEN, ok true,
  pairs 56, no key lost or gained against the pre-run register.

RED PROOF (the guard watched to fire, then restored):
  iceman/hero_back.png moved aside; `--sheet --only iceman --name _redproof`
  -> ok false, verdict RED,
     blank {files 2, expected_files 3, cells 1, scope named_subset,
            failures [[.../iceman/hero_back.png, "missing"]]}
     errors += "blank_check: opened 2 view PNGs but the sheet has 1 cells, so 1
